<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_escalation_rate" target="global_energy_shocks::chokepoint_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising kinetic operations (naval strikes, mining, missile strikes near ports and lanes) directly increase the probability of interruptions and hazards to merchant traffic transiting key maritime chokepoints (e.g., Black Sea access, Turkish Straits), raising disruption risk.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_shocks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_escalation_rate" target="global_financial_shift::bond_market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Spikes in kinetic escalation prompt rapid re‑pricing, safe‑haven rotations, and stop‑loss cascades that produce large short‑term moves in sovereign bond prices, raising bond‑market volatility.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_financial_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_escalation_rate" target="global_financial_shift::risk_premia_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained or intensified military action increases the perceived probability of sanctions, supply disruptions and fiscal strain for exposed states, so investors demand higher risk premia on sovereign debt.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_financial_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_escalation_rate" target="tech_ai_geopolitical_riv::compute_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Spikes in kinetic escalation prompt governments and vendors to extend export controls and self‑restrict shipments of high‑end accelerators (to avoid diversion or sanctions exposure), producing immediate shortages and reduced available accelerator‑hours for AI training.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">tech_ai_geopolitical_riv</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_escalation_rate" target="tech_ai_geopolitical_riv::data_center_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased strikes and kinetic risk near conflict zones lead cloud providers and investors to suspend construction, evacuate equipment, or decommission at‑risk facilities, directly reducing local data‑center capacity available for AI workloads.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">tech_ai_geopolitical_riv</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_escalation_rate" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::kinetic_military_pressur" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained Russian kinetic escalation forces U.S. and allied naval/air assets to be reallocated to Europe for deterrence and logistics, reducing available forward presence and routine kinetic pressure (patrols, strikes, escorts) in the Gulf theatre.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_escalation_rate" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::sanctions_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher Russian escalation increases Western sanctions on energy and shipping; Russia seeks alternative suppliers and evasion channels (including Iranian oil/shipping), prompting the U.S. and partners to broaden and intensify sanctions targeting Iran-linked intermediaries to block circumvention.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
