  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A shift in battlefield capabilities that enables capture or long-range strikes against adversary-held infrastructure leads to physical damage, occupation, or supply-line denial of refining plants and associated feedstock flows, reducing operational refinery capacity.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_shocks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_capability_bala" target="tech_ai_geopolitical_riv::ai_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A perceived shift in military capability in favor of the adversary drives governments and defense/strategic investors to accelerate procurement and funding for military and dual‑use AI firms, increasing private and public capital flows into AI development.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
