<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::threat_perception_levels" target="global_energy_shocks::wholesale_gas_price" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Elevated public and elite threat perceptions drive precautionary buying, stronger forward contracting and speculative activity, which push up benchmark wholesale gas prices under near-term supply uncertainty.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_shocks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::threat_perception_levels" target="global_financial_shift::market_policy_expectatio" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising public and elite threat perceptions raise the expected frequency of energy/supply shocks and fiscal support, causing markets to price in earlier and/or larger central‑bank tightening (shift toward tighter policy expectations).</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_financial_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::threat_perception_levels" target="tech_ai_geopolitical_riv::regulatory_stringency" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising public and elite threat perceptions push policymakers to rapidly introduce and enforce stricter export controls, vetting, and deployment restrictions on AI technologies for national security reasons, raising regulatory stringency.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">tech_ai_geopolitical_riv</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::threat_perception_levels" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::diplomatic_tension_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising public and elite threat perceptions from the Russia war heighten political incentives in Washington and allied capitals to adopt tougher public posture and formal complaints toward Iran and Gulf actors (e.g., accusing facilitation of Russian evasion or proxy collaboration), elevating diplomatic tensions in the region.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
