<edge source="global_energy_shocks::chokepoint_risk" target="global_financial_shift::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in shipping chokepoint risk raises perceived global trade and tail-risk, triggering portfolio shifts into developed-market sovereigns and increasing net capital inflows to those markets as safe-haven flows rise.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shocks</data>
  <data key="d40">global_financial_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shocks::chokepoint_risk" target="russia_ukraine_war::diplomatic_engagement_in" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising risk of disruptions at key maritime chokepoints (e.g., Black Sea approaches, Bosporus) triggers urgent multilateral diplomatic activity and coordination (mediators, coastal states, insurers) to reopen or secure sea lanes and resume export flows.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shocks</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shocks::chokepoint_risk" target="tech_ai_geopolitical_riv::compute_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher shipping chokepoint risk delays and reduces deliveries of accelerator hardware (GPUs/TPUs) and networking equipment, directly lowering immediately available high‑performance compute for training and large-scale inference.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shocks</data>
  <data key="d40">tech_ai_geopolitical_riv</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shocks::chokepoint_risk" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::oil_flow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in chokepoint disruption risk causes shipping firms and traders to reroute, slow transits, or cancel voyages and for insurers to raise premiums, producing an immediate measurable reduction in oil shipments through the affected route.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-3 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shocks</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
