<edge source="global_energy_shocks::wholesale_gas_price" target="global_financial_shift::market_policy_expectatio" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A rapid rise in wholesale gas prices feeds directly into near-term headline and core inflation readings, prompting market re-pricing of central bank tightening and thus raising market-implied probabilities of sooner/higher policy moves.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shocks</data>
  <data key="d40">global_financial_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shocks::wholesale_gas_price" target="russia_ukraine_war::negotiation_appetite" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in wholesale gas prices raises domestic energy bills and political pressure in European consumer states, pushing their governments toward supporting diplomatic compromises or expedited talks to restore stable supplies.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shocks</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shocks::wholesale_gas_price" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_capability_bala" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained higher gas prices increase export revenue flows to Russia, providing fiscal room for defense procurement, ammunition production and logistics support that shift the comparative military capability balance in Russia's favour within the procurement and sustainment timescale.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shocks</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shocks::wholesale_gas_price" target="tech_ai_geopolitical_riv::ai_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp increases in benchmark gas prices raise data‑center and energy costs and compress forecasted returns on capital‑intensive AI projects, prompting investors and firms to delay or reduce funding into AI model training and infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shocks</data>
  <data key="d40">tech_ai_geopolitical_riv</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shocks::wholesale_gas_price" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::kinetic_military_pressur" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp rises in wholesale gas prices increase urgency among consuming states and their militaries to secure sea lines and deter perceived disruptors, prompting higher tempo of patrols, interdictions, and kinetic signaling against actors in the Gulf region.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shocks</data>
