  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A shift in market-implied expectations toward tighter monetary policy raises discount rates and weakens near-term demand growth projections (and often strengthens the currency), which together lower forward and spot wholesale gas prices through repricing of futures and reduced consumption.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_shift</data>
