  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp increases in sovereign bond volatility signal acute fiscal or financial stress, prompting governments and regulators to accelerate or broaden interventions in energy markets (price caps, subsidies, export restrictions) to control inflation, protect consumers, or stabilize markets.</data>
