<edge source="global_financial_shift::cross_border_flows" target="global_energy_shocks::commercial_fuel_stocks" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in cross-border capital inflows provides trading houses and refiners with short-term funding and working-capital access to buy and hold crude and refined product inventories, directly raising commercial fuel stocks as purchases and forward roll activity expand.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_shocks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_financial_shift::cross_border_flows" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_capability_bala" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained inflows into developed-market sovereign debt lower borrowing costs and fiscal strain for Western donors, making it easier for them to finance and deliver weapons, ammunition, and sustainment to Ukraine, thereby improving Ukraine's relative military-capability balance versus Russia.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_financial_shift::cross_border_flows" target="tech_ai_geopolitical_riv::ai_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise/fall in net cross-border capital flows directly increases/decreases the pool of international VC, private equity and portfolio funding available to AI startups and scaleups, changing the rate of AI investment within a few fundraising cycles.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">tech_ai_geopolitical_riv</data>
</edge>
