<edge source="global_financial_shift::risk_premia_level" target="global_energy_shocks::commercial_fuel_stocks" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising sovereign risk premia increase the cost of carrying inventory and of short-term corporate borrowing, forcing fuel traders and refiners to liquidate or run down commercial stockpiles to reduce financing costs, lowering aggregate commercial fuel stocks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_shocks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_financial_shift::risk_premia_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::negotiation_appetite" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising global sovereign risk premia increase domestic economic and political costs for governments supporting a prolonged war, boosting political incentives to pursue negotiated settlements or de‑escalatory talks to avert further economic damage.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
